   Keywords and Filters Help
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This is one of the best features of this mail door.       What keywords,
   filters and twit settings allow you do to,  is 'fine tune' what messages
   you will receive,  and what messages to avoid.   You can save yourself a
   lot of time, first by not having to download such a huge mail packet and
   secondly because  you will not have to read a bunch of messages that are
   not of interest to you.

   Keywords are words  that are usually subject matters of interest to you.
   For example,  if you really liked a certain hockey team,  or movie star,
   you could place their name in a "Keyword" and the messages in areas that
   had been marked to apply keywords in, would be sent to you.  Filters are
   just the opposite.  If you really dislike a certain subject,  or message
   content,  then you can select it here,  and the message will be ignored.
   Twits are people  that no matter what  they write about,  it always is a
   waste of space as far as you are concerned - put their  name in the twit
   list and you will be sure not to have to read their dribble again.  Once
   your  settings are perfected,  you will enjoy  smaller packets with only
   messages that actually interest you.
 
